<div id="efficiencyCalculator" class="ec-layout">
  <div class="ec-main-column">
    <section class="cc-panel">
      <div class="ec-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="cc-label">01 · Score formula</p>
          <h2>Explore efficiency and volume</h2>
          <p class="ec-muted">Volume adds at most one fifth of the points left after efficiency.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ec-heading-actions">
          <span class="ec-lambda">λ = 0.2</span>
          <button id="copyEfficiencySummary" type="button" class="cc-action-btn">Copy Summary</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ec-explorer-grid">
        <label class="ec-slider-field">
          <span>Efficiency rating E <strong id="explorerEValue">0.50</strong></span>
          <input type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.01" value="0.5" data-explorer="e" aria-label="Efficiency rating E" />
        </label>
        <label class="ec-slider-field">
          <span>Volume rating V <strong id="explorerVValue">0.50</strong></span>
          <input type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.01" value="0.5" data-explorer="v" aria-label="Volume rating V" />
        </label>
      </div>
      <div id="scorePresets" class="ec-chip-row">
        <button type="button" data-example="typical" class="ec-chip">Typical</button>
        <button type="button" data-example="power" class="ec-chip">Power user</button>
        <button type="button" data-example="wasteful" class="ec-chip">Heavy but wasteful</button>
        <button type="button" data-example="careful" class="ec-chip">Careful, low volume</button>
      </div>
      <div class="ec-score-result">
        <code id="explorerFormula">100 × (0.50 + 0.2 × 0.50 × 0.50) = 55</code>
        <span class="ec-grade ec-grade-satisfactory" id="explorerGrade">Satisfactory</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ec-point-grid">
        <div><span>Base points, 100E</span><strong id="explorerBasePoints">50 points</strong></div>
        <div><span>Volume points</span><strong id="explorerVolumePoints">5 points</strong></div>
        <div><span>Maximum volume points</span><strong id="explorerMaxPoints">10 points</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cc-panel">
      <div class="ec-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="cc-label">02 · Team usage</p>
          <h2>Useful work and monthly spend</h2>
          <p class="ec-muted">Count sessions only when they produce useful work, such as a merged PR or a delivered non-PR outcome.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ec-actions">
          <button id="resetExamples" type="button" class="cc-action-btn">Reset to blog examples</button>
          <button id="addEngineer" type="button" class="cc-action-btn">Add row</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ec-column-labels" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>Engineer and monthly inputs</span>
        <span>Derived ratings and approval outcome</span>
      </div>
      <div id="engineerRows" class="ec-engineer-list"></div>
      <p class="ec-footnote">Up to 25 engineers. Rows are local to this page and are not saved.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="cc-panel">
      <div class="ec-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="cc-label">03 · Policy &amp; assumptions</p>
          <h2>Set team benchmarks and limits</h2>
          <p class="ec-muted">The post does not publish the saturation curve or score thresholds. These are editable assumptions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ec-settings-grid">
        <label class="ec-field"><span>Workdays per month</span><input type="number" min="1" step="1" data-setting="workdaysPerMonth" /></label>
        <label class="ec-field"><span>Benchmark $ / productive hour</span><input type="number" min="0.01" step="1" data-setting="benchmarkCostPerHour" /></label>
        <label class="ec-field"><span>Benchmark productive hours / day</span><input type="number" min="0.01" step="0.1" data-setting="benchmarkHoursPerDay" /></label>
        <label class="ec-field"><span>Engineer loaded cost / hour ($)</span><input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-setting="engineerHourlyCost" /></label>
        <label class="ec-field"><span>Base monthly limit ($)</span><input type="number" min="0" step="100" data-setting="baseMonthlyLimit" /></label>
        <label class="ec-field"><span>Auto-approval ceiling ($)</span><input type="number" min="0" step="100" data-setting="autoApproveCeiling" /></label>
        <label class="ec-field"><span>Healthy threshold</span><input type="number" min="0" max="100" step="1" data-setting="healthyThreshold" /></label>
        <label class="ec-field"><span>Satisfactory threshold</span><input type="number" min="0" max="100" step="1" data-setting="satisfactoryThreshold" /></label>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cc-panel ec-methodology">
      <p class="cc-label">Methodology</p>
      <h2>Published model and local assumptions</h2>
      <div class="ec-method-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>From the post</h3>
          <p>The score is 100 × (E + λ·V·(1 − E)), with λ = 0.2. Volume can contribute no more than one fifth of the points not already earned through efficiency. Count only sessions with useful work, such as a merged PR or a delivered outcome for non-PR work. The policy uses Healthy, Satisfactory, Needs Improvement, and Unknown grades. Healthy and Satisfactory can receive automatic limit increases up to the admin-set ceiling. Requests above that ceiling and requests from other grades go to an admin. The policy does not auto-deny.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Assumptions used here</h3>
          <p>The E and V curves use 1 − 2^(−x / benchmark), so each benchmark corresponds to a 0.50 rating. Defaults are $40 per productive hour, 1.5 productive hours per workday, 65 / 50 grade thresholds, and at least 5 sessions for a grade. Hours under each cap are estimated linearly per dollar. Spend pending admin review is not counted as approved spend or productive hours.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <aside class="cc-panel ec-summary" aria-labelledby="efficiency-summary-title">
    <p class="cc-label">Team snapshot</p>
    <h2 id="efficiency-summary-title">Efficiency summary</h2>
    <dl class="ec-summary-list">
      <div><dt>Total spend</dt><dd id="summarySpend">$19,956</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Productive hours</dt><dd id="summaryHours">329.8 h</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Blended cost / productive hour</dt><dd id="summaryBlendedCost">$60.51/h</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Value delivered and ROI</dt><dd id="summaryValue">$32,980 · 1.65x ROI</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Spend without useful work</dt><dd id="summaryWastedSpend">$9,588</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Grade distribution</dt><dd id="summaryGrades">1 Healthy · 2 Satisfactory · 1 Needs Improvement · 0 Unknown</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Average score</dt><dd id="summaryAverage">58</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="ec-summary-divider"></div>
    <h3>Blanket cap vs efficiency-based approvals</h3>
    <dl class="ec-summary-list">
      <div><dt>Hours under blanket cap</dt><dd id="summaryBlanketHours">70.1 h</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Hours under efficiency policy</dt><dd id="summaryPolicyHours">197.1 h</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Hours unlocked</dt><dd id="summaryUnlockedHours">127 h</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Auto-approved spend</dt><dd id="summaryAutoApproved">$5,080</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Spend in admin queue</dt><dd id="summaryAdminQueue">$11,700 · 1 engineer</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="ec-summary-note">Admin-pending spend is not treated as granted. Approval outcomes are estimates from the selected limits and grades.</p>
  </aside>
</div>

<style is:global>
